    "coordinates": "Metres, +Y up, model fronts face +Z. Each asset node has its origin at the centre of its footprint on the ground (y = 0); every root node has an identity transform (except skyline.glb, whose nodes carry a suggested world placement).",
    "nodeLookup": "Layout buildings map to node `${kind}_v${variant}`. Facilities that exist twice with different footprints (pump-station, water-tower) have one node per facility: resolve by assets[].facilityId first, then by kind + variant.",
    "kitScaling": "Kit buildings (tower-residential, tower-office, midrise-residential, lowrise-residential, villa, commercial-podium) are modelled at nominalSize [w, d, h] and tolerate non-uniform scaling of about +/-30% to the layout footprint/height. Facility, prop and underground assets are modelled at real size and placed unscaled.",
    "glazing": "Material \"glazing\" marks window surfaces for the scene's lit-window shader. UV0 on glazing encodes the window grid: v = storey coordinate (the lobby spans v 0..1, every storey above adds 1.0, aligned with the modelled slabs, so fract(v) is the position inside a storey even after non-uniform scaling); u = facade bay coordinate (1.0 per ~1.5-3 m bay, see assets[].notes). World-space window shaders also work.",
    "vertexAO": "Building, facility and underground meshes carry baked ambient occlusion in COLOR_0 (linear, 0.38-1.0). three.js GLTFLoader enables vertexColors automatically, which multiplies baseColor. Keep vertexColors on any replacement material to keep the grounding.",
    "compression": "EXT_meshopt_compression (decode with GLTFLoader.setMeshoptDecoder(MeshoptDecoder) from three/examples/jsm/libs/meshopt_decoder.module.js). Normals are int16 and COLOR_0 uint8 (KHR_mesh_quantization); positions and UVs are float32.",
    "emissive": "Emissive materials (\"emissive_sign\", \"light_emissive\", \"water\") carry emissive colour/strength suitable for bloom; the scene may drive their intensity (e.g. night/outage states).",
    "pipes": "Exposed mains are rendered by the scene from district.json routes. district-base gallery saddles and underground-kit flanges are sized for a visual pipe radius of 0.9 m (anchors.pipeVisualRadius).",
    "provenance": "All assets are original procedural geometry and textures generated for Encirra by the scripts in assets/blender/. No third-party models, textures or HDRIs are used."
